From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:26:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] bls: Pick the default entry from loader.conf

m1n1 is the boot loader of these devices and should start the right
system by itself, as systemd-boot does on a PC. Pick the default the way
systemd-boot does without EFI variables: the default line of
/loader/loader.conf is a glob (for example "default omarchy-4d6c1a2b-*",
one system's entries), matched against each entry id with or without
.conf; the first match in BLS order is the default, which is the newest
kernel of that system, bootable or not. Without loader.conf, a default
line or a match, the first bootable entry is. The last default line
wins, a pair of quotes around the value goes, and every other key
(timeout, editor and so on) is ignored: there is no menu on the device.
An unreadable loader.conf is ignored with a line on the console.

P_BOOT_ENTRIES marks the default with a "default yes" line in its block.
The contract stays 1: hosts keep keys they don't know. Without a DTB
file name from the caller, entries are now checked against the board
m1n1 runs on, any *-BOARD.dtb for its ADT target-type, so m1n1 judges
them the same with or without a host. P_BOOT_START refuses a missing
entry id; the default is for m1n1 itself to start.

